From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 18:26:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iio: proximity: vl53l0x-i2c: select the triggered buffer
 support it uses

The driver sets up a triggered buffer and allocates its own trigger when
it has an interrupt, but its Kconfig entry selects neither, unlike
VL53L1X_I2C next to it. With IIO_TRIGGERED_BUFFER disabled, as in the
arm64 defconfig-derived config this was found in, the module references
symbols nothing provides.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/iio/proximity/Kconfig | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/proximity/Kconfig b/drivers/iio/proximity/Kconfig
index bb77fad2a1b3..0793a530f70d 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/proximity/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/iio/proximity/Kconfig
@@ -236,6 +236,8 @@ config VCNL3020
 config VL53L0X_I2C
 	tristate "STMicroelectronics VL53L0X ToF ranger sensor (I2C)"
 	depends on I2C
+	select IIO_BUFFER
+	select IIO_TRIGGERED_BUFFER
 	help
 	  Say Y here to build a driver for STMicroelectronics VL53L0X
 	  ToF ranger sensors with i2c interface.
